  "description": "This easy 5-minute apple raita combines crisp, sweet-tart apple with creamy yogurt, cumin, and Kashmiri chile for a cooling, crunchy side.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Finely chopped fresh cilantro leaves and tender stems, for serving (optional)\n\nNotes: This recipe can easily be doubled.\nKashmiri chile powder, available at Indian grocery stores and online, has moderate heat, a slightly fruity flavor, and a vibrant red color. If unavailable, substitute sweet paprika with a pinch of cayenne.\nGrate the apple just before serving to minimize browning.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The yogurt mixture can be prepared through step 1 up to 4 days in advance and refrigerated in an airtight container.\nApple raita is best enjoyed shortly after it’s made while the apple is still crisp and vibrant, but leftovers can be safely refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 4 days.",
